Answer: (D) {−3,−2,−1,1,2,3}
Why and working: The condition excludes zero and allows integer magnitudes 1, 2 and 3, since 3²=9 but 4²=16.
Why not the others: (A) misses negative integers. (B) includes the excluded zero. (C) misses the magnitude 3.

Answer: (B) {4k+3 : k∈ℤ}
Why and working: Write a+1=4j, so a=4j−1=4(j−1)+3. All and only these integers are related.
Why not the others: (A) uses the wrong sign of the residue. (C) contains multiples of four rather than the required residue. (D) uses an order condition rather than divisibility.
